&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Camera Hardware &amp;amp; Calibration:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Hands-on experience configuring and calibrating mainstream 2D area-scan/line-scan cameras (e.g.Basler) and 3D sensors (e.g.Intel RealSense, structured-light cameras), including nine-point, checkerboard, and 3D hand-eye calibration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vision Algorithms:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Understanding of&amp;nbsp;the underlying logic of vision-based AGV navigation — QR-code navigation and natural-contour navigation (V-SLAM) — as well as the deployment of deep-learning-based detection models (e.g.the YOLO series).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programming &amp;amp; Scripting:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Good C++ and Python programming skills, with the ability to make API calls and perform simple secondary development based on vision vendor SDKs; proficient in Python for automated test scripts and data-log processing; comfortable working in Linux (Ubuntu) environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industrial Communication:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Ability to configure data exchange between vision IPCs and PLCs; understanding of TCP/IP socket communication, Modbus TCP, and ROS/ROS2 inter-node communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;High motivation and curiosity to quickly learn&amp;nbsp;new technologies, tools, and industrial vision applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Willingness to Travel:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Willingness to travel to customer sites (domestic and international) for on-site commissioning activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Good communication&amp;nbsp;skills in English/German&amp;nbsp;and the ability to work hands-on in an international team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
